{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>I have heard.</b> The word תְּלוּנָּה is unique; it has a dagesh in the nun, and this prophecy is repeated, for Moses had already mentioned it in 'HaShem will give you in the evening flesh to eat, and bread in the morning' (verse 8); only it was repeated for Israel's sake, so that they would see the Glory:" "And the phrase בֵּין הָעַרְבַּיִם is like בָּעֶרֶב, as I explained. And from this verse the meaning of 'and in the morning you shall see the Glory of YHWH' (verse 7) is clarified, for here it is written: 'between the evenings you shall eat flesh, and in the morning you shall be sated with bread.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:04.995328051Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}